From bd2a5f5503351b311d61d0a540157ce5cb22cab1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaozhi-local <local@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:07:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sub: keep color bitmaps off the text layer

The color emoji support makes a track that contains one colored bitmap
render the *whole* subtitle layer as BGRA, and the BGRA path blends every
pixel in software while the coverage path is a memcpy per bitmap. Measured
on the user's setup (3072x1920, fullscreen danmaku, 20 s): the same content
costs 5.4 s CPU as Y8 and 19.3 s as merged BGRA, with only ~15% of the ink
actually colored.

So split the two: color bitmaps get their own BGRA layer (a new OSD object
type next to the primary subtitle track, so it has its own VO cache slot and
draws between the text and the OSD), and everything else goes back to the
coverage format. --force-rgba-osd-rendering, VOs that cannot do Y8, the OSD
layer, script overlays and the secondary track keep the single merged layer
they had; tracks without color bitmaps are unaffected either.
---
